findings.description:
Scope excludes "viewer/client rendering optimization". Each tier nonetheless requires a "demonstrable artifact". The wire design also requires client changes:

- interpolation for the 30 Hz stream;
- delta decode and resync;
- the camera control channel;
- biome shading "before or alongside the 50k milestone";
- rendering 50k+ instances.

Initiative 600 (Client Layer) is `not_started` and is not listed as a dependency. The 250k–2M tiers also assume "~50k visible at ground level" with a plain frustum. No occlusion, far-plane or aggregate fallback is given. For a camera inside a dense 2D collision, that bound is asserted, not derived.
